Thus we need to create origin_availability_alpha as candidate_entity, allocate vehicle, attach task profile, confirm preparedness, assign operator, etc.

Similarly for destination? Not needed for goal but maybe needed for transport leg assembly.

Goal only requires dispatched origin_availability_alpha, not destination_availability_alpha.

But to assemble transport leg we may need origin_availability_locked and destination_availability_locked (for assemble_transport_leg). However mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready requires origin_availability_locked and origin_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_assembled, transport_leg_loading_authorized. It does not require destination_availability_locked. So we can assemble transport leg with just origin availability? Actually assemble_transport_leg requires both origin_availability_locked and destination_availability_locked. But we may not need to assemble transport leg if we use assemble_origin_loaded_leg etc? Those also require both origin and destination locked. However mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready requires transport_leg_assembled (any assembly). So we need to assemble a transport leg. The assemble actions require both origin and destination locked. So we need to lock destination availability as well, even if not needed for goal. But we can lock destination availability similarly (through prepare destination, assign operator, lock destination). That may add extra steps but necessary.

Thus we need to prepare both origin and destination availabilities (as candidate_entities) to lock them, assemble transport leg, authorize loading, then mark origin availability dispatch ready, allocate dispatch slot, execute origin dispatch.

Similarly for shift_candidate_alpha we need to dispatch it as schedule candidate; that may require similar steps but maybe we can reuse some steps (like transport leg assembled etc). For shift_candidate_alpha dispatch readiness we can use finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation (which gives dispatch_ready). That does not require transport leg assembly. So we might not need to assemble transport leg for shift_candidate_alpha. Indeed finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation only requires compliance_validation_complete. So we can dispatch shift_candidate_alpha without needing transport leg assembly. Good.

Thus we can focus on preparing shift_candidate_alpha for dispatch via compliance path, and preparing origin_availability_alpha for dispatch via lock and mark dispatch ready (which needs transport leg assembled). That means we need to prepare destination availability as well to assemble transport leg.

